The compiler and its tools are comp's: the base and man lists no longer name them.

EmiBSD's toolchain is DevTools' LLVM, laid into the system from its artifact, and it goes in
the comp set whole (the user's decisions of 2026-11-08 and 2026-11-15). The base lists named
the compiler's drivers and the object tools (cc, c++, cpp, clang, clang++, clang-cpp, ld,
ld.lld, ar, nm, objcopy, size, strings, strip), which there are links to programs comp
carries, and the man list five of their pages. They leave both; comp's list of the compiler
is written from the artifact by the build (tools/world.py) and names them. The C++ run time
and the compiler's run time (libc++.so, libc++abi.so, libcompiler_rt.a) stay in base.

